(3431527, 474948, 53316, '<td valign="top">I generally do not prefer small DOF because a lot of times it seems like it is used just for the sake of using it. But here, it really adds to the photo - and adds to it in a very wonderful way, I think.  This was a ten from me!</td>', 'I generally do not prefer small DOF because a lot of times it seems like it is used just for the sake of using it. But here, it really adds to the photo - and adds to it in a very wonderful way, I think.  This was a ten from me!', '2007-03-05 17:37:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(3431539, 475287, 53316, '<td valign="top">I love the saturated colors.</td>', 'I love the saturated colors.', '2007-03-05 17:39:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(3431544, 475008, 68256, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyone.  This was my first attempt at a high key portrait.  It took me two days and lots of fiddling to get the light like I wanted it and about 30 seconds to take the picture.  I''m glad it was well received.</td>', 'Thanks everyone.  This was my first attempt at a high key portrait.  It took me two days and lots of fiddling to get the light like I wanted it and about 30 seconds to take the picture.  I''m glad it was well received.', '2007-03-05 17:42:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(3431588, 472894, 44878, '<td valign="top">Well Done Ian.<br/>I think your beggining to understand more about this site<br/>and think outside the Box.<br/>Congratulations on what I think is a cracking Photo.<br/> <br/>Joe</td>', 'Well Done Ian.I think your beggining to understand more about this siteand think outside the Box.Congratulations on what I think is a cracking Photo. Joe', '2007-03-05 18:03:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(3431642, 475107, 811, '<td valign="top">I didn''t get to vote on this one, but I remember seeing it and thinking, "what a cool idea."  My only suggestion would be to tilt it at some absurd angle to give it a little more drama, but, then again, I like things kinda off kilter.</td>', 'I didn''t get to vote on this one, but I remember seeing it and thinking, "what a cool idea."  My only suggestion would be to tilt it at some absurd angle to give it a little more drama, but, then again, I like things kinda off kilter.', '2007-03-05 18:23:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(3431653, 474248, 811, '<td valign="top">To me, this shot is one of showing compassion.  I know some people contract AIDS as a result of their lifestyle, but there are also innocents that get it, too.  And, regardless of how they got it, they are still people who are hurting.  In my life, I''ve known about AIDS since before it had a name.  I remember my uncle (who now has AIDS), my mother, and my grandmother talking in hushed worried voices about another "friend" that had "that disease that they don''t know what it is, what causes it, or how to cure it."  It would be two or three years later before it had a name. Thirty years later, there is still no cure, but we should be willing to give a hand to help however we can.  Great image.<br/> <br/></td>', 'To me, this shot is one of showing compassion.  I know some people contract AIDS as a result of their lifestyle, but there are also innocents that get it, too.  And, regardless of how they got it, they are still people who are hurting.  In my life, I''ve known about AIDS since before it had a name.  I remember my uncle (who now has AIDS), my mother, and my grandmother talking in hushed worried voices about another "friend" that had "that disease that they don''t know what it is, what causes it, or how to cure it."  It would be two or three years later before it had a name. Thirty years later, there is still no cure, but we should be willing to give a hand to help however we can.  Great image. ', '2007-03-05 18:28:18.000000', NULL, 0);
