(3431701, 473648, 44877, '<td valign="top">Sandy, I didn''t vote on this challenge, but I did browse through and this popped out as my favorite! I''m glad to see it''s yours!! Great job, great catch - very cute. It made me "LOL" right away!</td>', 'Sandy, I didn''t vote on this challenge, but I did browse through and this popped out as my favorite! I''m glad to see it''s yours!! Great job, great catch - very cute. It made me "LOL" right away!', '2007-03-05 18:50:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(3431717, 472905, 51538, '<td valign="top">I''ll make your 7th comment so that one out of three of your predictions, at least, comes true.  You would have done much better strongly backlighting the NIC - at least some IC boards have translucent areas which glow nicely with backlight.  Failing that, a mirror would help with a screen backlighting with some sort of binary digital motif bokeh and some directional lighting on the top of the NIC.  Value for money?  I have played around with various MBs and IC boards to reasonably profitable effect.</td>', 'I''ll make your 7th comment so that one out of three of your predictions, at least, comes true.  You would have done much better strongly backlighting the NIC - at least some IC boards have translucent areas which glow nicely with backlight.  Failing that, a mirror would help with a screen backlighting with some sort of binary digital motif bokeh and some directional lighting on the top of the NIC.  Value for money?  I have played around with various MBs and IC boards to reasonably profitable effect.', '2007-03-05 19:01:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(3431726, 475273, 51538, '<td valign="top">SEARCH was lost to me - and still is.  But who cares?  This is a pristine image.  Very pleasant.</td>', 'SEARCH was lost to me - and still is.  But who cares?  This is a pristine image.  Very pleasant.', '2007-03-05 19:08:25.000000', NULL, 0),
