(3433255, 475109, 30982, '<td valign="top">And here I was trying to figure out what was missing.  This is what happens when a military person who thinks acronyms literally is thrown for a loop.  I thought perhaps a horse had escaped the barn, or the title referred to the missing panels in the door.  I did, however, like all the red (one challenge too early!), the lines, and the snow falling.</td>', 'And here I was trying to figure out what was missing.  This is what happens when a military person who thinks acronyms literally is thrown for a loop.  I thought perhaps a horse had escaped the barn, or the title referred to the missing panels in the door.  I did, however, like all the red (one challenge too early!), the lines, and the snow falling.', '2007-03-06 09:00:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(3433259, 474180, 30982, '<td valign="top">I figured this was probably yours.  :-)  Interesting point about requiring a tripod, though in their defense, I suspect it''s a safety thing more than anything.  Tripods can be tripping hazards and in a place like a metro, you''d rather not have folks falling into each other.  Your shots from DC make me kinda sad I wasn''t "into" photography when I lived in northern Virginia.</td>', 'I figured this was probably yours.  :-)  Interesting point about requiring a tripod, though in their defense, I suspect it''s a safety thing more than anything.  Tripods can be tripping hazards and in a place like a metro, you''d rather not have folks falling into each other.  Your shots from DC make me kinda sad I wasn''t "into" photography when I lived in northern Virginia.', '2007-03-06 09:03:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(3433260, 473888, 30982, '<td valign="top">Heh - I didn''t recognize Octopussy with only the normal number of legs.  I still think this is a hoot of a picture!</td>', 'Heh - I didn''t recognize Octopussy with only the normal number of legs.  I still think this is a hoot of a picture!', '2007-03-06 09:05:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(3433265, 473939, 30982, '<td valign="top">A very good choice for the challenge and while I think the vignetting is appropriate, I do think it''s just a bit too strong, covering too much of the picture.  Very good post processing!!  Appreciate you including that in your comments, too.</td>', 'A very good choice for the challenge and while I think the vignetting is appropriate, I do think it''s just a bit too strong, covering too much of the picture.  Very good post processing!!  Appreciate you including that in your comments, too.', '2007-03-06 09:07:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(3433269, 472905, 30982, '<td valign="top">Appears to me to be a good clean product shot.  I like the angle you chose.  About the only thing I''d suggest (and pineapple''s suggestions are the ones you should go with anyway) is to "whiten" the white a bit more - seems a bit bluish cast to me.</td>', 'Appears to me to be a good clean product shot.  I like the angle you chose.  About the only thing I''d suggest (and pineapple''s suggestions are the ones you should go with anyway) is to "whiten" the white a bit more - seems a bit bluish cast to me.', '2007-03-06 09:10:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(3433274, 472553, 30982, '<td valign="top">I was about to scold your for shooting while driving until I read your comment!  Good, clean shot, depicted the acronym well.  The light indicating "Drive" is a tad overbright, maybe.</td>', 'I was about to scold your for shooting while driving until I read your comment!  Good, clean shot, depicted the acronym well.  The light indicating "Drive" is a tad overbright, maybe.', '2007-03-06 09:11:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(3433279, 475348, 30982, '<td valign="top">I''d guess most of the non-US voters didn''t know what BLM is - and for that matter, those that don''t live or haven''t lived in the western part of the country may not know.  But for those of us who HAVE lived in the west, this is a pretty good pictoral description.  I do like the creative things people came up with, though!  And I''ll agree that maybe something providing foreground interest would perk this up a bit.  But as for descibing the acronym, it works as is!</td>', 'I''d guess most of the non-US voters didn''t know what BLM is - and for that matter, those that don''t live or haven''t lived in the western part of the country may not know.  But for those of us who HAVE lived in the west, this is a pretty good pictoral description.  I do like the creative things people came up with, though!  And I''ll agree that maybe something providing foreground interest would perk this up a bit.  But as for descibing the acronym, it works as is!', '2007-03-06 09:14:14.000000', NULL, 0),
