(3446792, 475293, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"EPA" was a good entry into the Acronyms challenge.  I think you did  a good job starting with a acronym that most can recognize and understand.  <br/> <br/>This is a very nice photo, great timing catching the deer and bird in their natural environment.  I think the composition is very nice, I might have tried to leave the very top of the tree on the right hand side.  Also I think I might have tried to increase the contrast or balance a little to really draw out the elements in this great photo.  <br/> <br/>The focus looks very nice along with the lighting, you could have easily over blown the snow.  Very good work!</td>', '*Critique Club* "EPA" was a good entry into the Acronyms challenge.  I think you did  a good job starting with a acronym that most can recognize and understand.   This is a very nice photo, great timing catching the deer and bird in their natural environment.  I think the composition is very nice, I might have tried to leave the very top of the tree on the right hand side.  Also I think I might have tried to increase the contrast or balance a little to really draw out the elements in this great photo.   The focus looks very nice along with the lighting, you could have easily over blown the snow.  Very good work!', '2007-03-09 15:13:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(3446807, 475340, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"WIG" is a very cool entry into the Acronyms challenge, I wasn''t sure what the acronym was but the photo was very cool.  <br/> <br/>Now seeing that WIG means wine in a glass it makes sense, honestly not knowing for sure what it was did not take away from my score. <br/> <br/> <br/>Excellent idea with the Jello, I am sure most of us out here would not have thought of this.  The photo is a very clean shot, the white is immaculate.  The red creates prefect lines to grab the eye.  Looking at your photo now  the only I see is on the third glass there is a small reflection but I think most of us would not have seen it.  <br/> <br/>Awesome job on the creativity!!</td>', '*Critique Club* "WIG" is a very cool entry into the Acronyms challenge, I wasn''t sure what the acronym was but the photo was very cool.   Now seeing that WIG means wine in a glass it makes sense, honestly not knowing for sure what it was did not take away from my score.   Excellent idea with the Jello, I am sure most of us out here would not have thought of this.  The photo is a very clean shot, the white is immaculate.  The red creates prefect lines to grab the eye.  Looking at your photo now  the only I see is on the third glass there is a small reflection but I think most of us would not have seen it.   Awesome job on the creativity!!', '2007-03-09 15:23:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(3446831, 473888, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"DNMC - Do Not Mock Cat!" is a different entry into the Acronyms challenge. I am really glad that you spelled out your acronym some entries were too hard to tell what they meant.<br/> <br/>Birman is giving us that look I have seen my mom''s Himalayan makes when he is not getting what he wants. I think if we have a little more focus on him, right in the nose it might have helped.  Also I might have tried to shoot with a plainer background and surrounding, so we can focus only on him.  <br/> <br/>Overall I think you did a good job coming up with an acronym we all now and making it fun.</td>', '*Critique Club* "DNMC - Do Not Mock Cat!" is a different entry into the Acronyms challenge. I am really glad that you spelled out your acronym some entries were too hard to tell what they meant. Birman is giving us that look I have seen my mom''s Himalayan makes when he is not getting what he wants. I think if we have a little more focus on him, right in the nose it might have helped.  Also I might have tried to shoot with a plainer background and surrounding, so we can focus only on him.   Overall I think you did a good job coming up with an acronym we all now and making it fun.', '2007-03-09 15:33:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(3446856, 474796, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"WTF???" is a prefect entry into the acronym challenge, something we all know and have said a bunch of times. You also did a great job of capturing the acronym appropriately.  <br/> <br/>I think you made an excellent choice of going black and white to really grab the viewers attention in at your eyes.  The lighting and contrast both look very good. I am really surprised that you didn''t score higher, this really is a great piece for the challenge. Honestly I am not sure why you didn''t place higher.  Maybe voters are a little burned out on the self portraits, I am not sure.  <br/> <br/>Overall great piece and good job on the self portrait!</td>', '*Critique Club* "WTF???" is a prefect entry into the acronym challenge, something we all know and have said a bunch of times. You also did a great job of capturing the acronym appropriately.   I think you made an excellent choice of going black and white to really grab the viewers attention in at your eyes.  The lighting and contrast both look very good. I am really surprised that you didn''t score higher, this really is a great piece for the challenge. Honestly I am not sure why you didn''t place higher.  Maybe voters are a little burned out on the self portraits, I am not sure.   Overall great piece and good job on the self portrait!', '2007-03-09 15:44:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(3446866, 475373, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"WTH ? ? ?" is a great entry into the acronym challenge, I remember seeing this while voting and thinking that this was an excellent entry.  <br/> <br/>Great post processing, it really lets the viewer focus on the subject.  I really like the focus glow on her face.  You did a wonderful job capturing that expression of confusion that we all have felt.  The lighting is very good and I like how you burned out the outside.  Also good work not capturing any reflection of her glasses. <br/> <br/>Overall, excellent work and congrats on placing 25th!</td>', '*Critique Club* "WTH ? ? ?" is a great entry into the acronym challenge, I remember seeing this while voting and thinking that this was an excellent entry.   Great post processing, it really lets the viewer focus on the subject.  I really like the focus glow on her face.  You did a wonderful job capturing that expression of confusion that we all have felt.  The lighting is very good and I like how you burned out the outside.  Also good work not capturing any reflection of her glasses.  Overall, excellent work and congrats on placing 25th!', '2007-03-09 15:53:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(3446894, 475277, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"IRS" is a good entry into the acronym challenge, unfortunately in most cases we all are extremely familiar with this one, especially this time of year.  <br/> <br/>I think you have created a very nice and clean shot.  The lighting and focus both look very nice.  I think between the negative feeling with IRS and the fact the image is not very out of the box as some of the entries the score was affected.  <br/> <br/>Nice work.</td>', '*Critique Club* "IRS" is a good entry into the acronym challenge, unfortunately in most cases we all are extremely familiar with this one, especially this time of year.   I think you have created a very nice and clean shot.  The lighting and focus both look very nice.  I think between the negative feeling with IRS and the fact the image is not very out of the box as some of the entries the score was affected.   Nice work.', '2007-03-09 16:04:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(3446979, 475266, 50695, '<td valign="top">Greetings From the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Sorry, it''s just me. :) I had fun guessing the acronym, but I had the same impression that Melethia had. It feels like you just pointed the camera at something. Now that''s not too bad a thing when it''s something important like this, but it dooms you to 5-land, and the soft focus dooms you to 4-land. You should always think about what is surrounding your subject, and you can change that by changing the angle of the shot and how close in you get.<br/> <br/>Your camera settings make me think it wasn''t as bright out as you thought. Notice your aperture is at 2.7. That creates a pretty shallow depth of field, and therefore not much is in focus. Are you aware of the sacred triangle of ISO, shutter speed, and aperture? If not, let me know and I''ll point you to a tutorial or write one myself.<br/> <br/>Sorry if I''m just giving you basic advice, but I''m pretty basic myself. :)</td>', 'Greetings From the Critique Club! Sorry, it''s just me. :) I had fun guessing the acronym, but I had the same impression that Melethia had. It feels like you just pointed the camera at something. Now that''s not too bad a thing when it''s something important like this, but it dooms you to 5-land, and the soft focus dooms you to 4-land. You should always think about what is surrounding your subject, and you can change that by changing the angle of the shot and how close in you get. Your camera settings make me think it wasn''t as bright out as you thought. Notice your aperture is at 2.7. That creates a pretty shallow depth of field, and therefore not much is in focus. Are you aware of the sacred triangle of ISO, shutter speed, and aperture? If not, let me know and I''ll point you to a tutorial or write one myself. Sorry if I''m just giving you basic advice, but I''m pretty basic myself. :)', '2007-03-09 16:41:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(3448278, 473896, 46177, '<td valign="top">Wow this really was a great shot, to bad it got DQ''d but doesn''t matter its still amazing no matter what!  Adding this one to my favorites!</td>', 'Wow this really was a great shot, to bad it got DQ''d but doesn''t matter its still amazing no matter what!  Adding this one to my favorites!', '2007-03-10 08:51:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(3449288, 474945, 45194, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB COMMENT<br/> <br/>I like the lighting on this shot and I think you came close to acheiving what you wanted to acheive. The model is well toned and you hit the shadows nearly perfectly to enhance definition.  Unfortunately the crop bothers me.  Having half the face in the photo seems ackward in my opinion.  I would have rather had from the neck down or all of the face - either or.  Having the lower part of the face in the shot also makes the model feel like he''s leaning, almost hunching forward. The models pose seems a little uncomfortable to me, as if he isn''t real relaxed.  Maybe resting a hand on the hip and shifting his weight to one leg or another would have helped. It seems the model is standing flat footed and it leads to a stiff looking pose.  The hairy legs are distracting for me because hsi chest is clean shaven and the hair on the legs draws me downward. Being a male commenter the last thing I want on this photo is my attention to be drawn downward! LOL.  Anyway, I think you were trying to duplicate a style of Calvin Klein ads here and for that you did a good job. Keep up the good work!</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB COMMENT I like the lighting on this shot and I think you came close to acheiving what you wanted to acheive. The model is well toned and you hit the shadows nearly perfectly to enhance definition.  Unfortunately the crop bothers me.  Having half the face in the photo seems ackward in my opinion.  I would have rather had from the neck down or all of the face - either or.  Having the lower part of the face in the shot also makes the model feel like he''s leaning, almost hunching forward. The models pose seems a little uncomfortable to me, as if he isn''t real relaxed.  Maybe resting a hand on the hip and shifting his weight to one leg or another would have helped. It seems the model is standing flat footed and it leads to a stiff looking pose.  The hairy legs are distracting for me because hsi chest is clean shaven and the hair on the legs draws me downward. Being a male commenter the last thing I want on this photo is my attention to be drawn downward! LOL.  Anyway, I think you were trying to duplicate a style of Calvin Klein ads here and for that you did a good job. Keep up the good work!', '2007-03-10 19:21:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(3449417, 474945, 15711, '<td valign="top">This is really a great shot.  I''m sure because of the "nature" of it, the nerd brigade was put off by it.  I think it''s well done.</td>', 'This is really a great shot.  I''m sure because of the "nature" of it, the nerd brigade was put off by it.  I think it''s well done.', '2007-03-10 20:18:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(3449576, 475333, 66384, '<td valign="top">Catherine, you''re adorable with your eyelashes and lipstick, and you''re quite the actress. Really, this was a great idea, and is such a fun photo. BTW, I like the "harsh direct lighting". It is appropriate to the scene -- someone reading in bed.</td>', 'Catherine, you''re adorable with your eyelashes and lipstick, and you''re quite the actress. Really, this was a great idea, and is such a fun photo. BTW, I like the "harsh direct lighting". It is appropriate to the scene -- someone reading in bed.', '2007-03-10 21:51:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(3450417, 471733, 16197, '<td valign="top"><b>From the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>How are you doing today?  I am going to touch on a few items with your image.<br/> <br/><b>Colour</b>;<br/>I really enjoy the colours here.  The balance of the reds within the transition as well as the white lights creates a strong form.  Along with the bits of yellow, blue, green inside gives the wandering eye something else to look at.<br/> <br/><b>DOF/Focus</b>;<br/>I like the focus here, being have to see the wet brick is very important for this image I believe.  Being wet adds a unique element.  The sign itself, it is hard to determine if it is in focus or slightly off because it is neon.  Overall this image holds strong focus for me.<br/> <br/><b>Post</b>;<br/>I don''t miss the clock so it was a good call to remove it, and it appears you have a good feel for the exposure/curves/usm you applied.  The image does not seem blown out or overly dark in any areas and most important the image is not flat either.<br/> <br/><b>Off Items</b>;<br/>I really enjoy this perspective, however, the tilting of the sign throws me.  I understand you had to shoot at an angle to get the manhole and the sign, However, Maybe a stronger rotation of the camera to make the sign even more angled.  For me it just throws me a bit.  Also, because the smaller signs are straight.<br/> <br/><b>Other</b>;<br/>As I continue to look through this image, I really enjoy the vanishing point created with the green pillars and light.  I am thinking if you cropped it off on the outside edge of the outside pillar (getting rid of that yellow cone on the far left) and changing perspective of the sign to make it straight horizontal this image would have a much more dramatic appeal.<br/> <br/>A very nice image and very fun concept for the challenge.  And well, it also makes me miss Wa. a bit.<br/> <br/>Nice Job<br/> <br/>Andrew ''littlegett''</td>', 'From the Critique Club  How are you doing today?  I am going to touch on a few items with your image. Colour;I really enjoy the colours here.  The balance of the reds within the transition as well as the white lights creates a strong form.  Along with the bits of yellow, blue, green inside gives the wandering eye something else to look at. DOF/Focus;I like the focus here, being have to see the wet brick is very important for this image I believe.  Being wet adds a unique element.  The sign itself, it is hard to determine if it is in focus or slightly off because it is neon.  Overall this image holds strong focus for me. Post;I don''t miss the clock so it was a good call to remove it, and it appears you have a good feel for the exposure/curves/usm you applied.  The image does not seem blown out or overly dark in any areas and most important the image is not flat either. Off Items;I really enjoy this perspective, however, the tilting of the sign throws me.  I understand you had to shoot at an angle to get the manhole and the sign, However, Maybe a stronger rotation of the camera to make the sign even more angled.  For me it just throws me a bit.  Also, because the smaller signs are straight. Other;As I continue to look through this image, I really enjoy the vanishing point created with the green pillars and light.  I am thinking if you cropped it off on the outside edge of the outside pillar (getting rid of that yellow cone on the far left) and changing perspective of the sign to make it straight horizontal this image would have a much more dramatic appeal. A very nice image and very fun concept for the challenge.  And well, it also makes me miss Wa. a bit. Nice Job Andrew ''littlegett''', '2007-03-11 13:47:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(3450440, 473826, 16197, '<td valign="top"><b>From the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>How are you doing today?  I am going to touch on a few items with your image.<br/> <br/><b>Colour</b>;<br/>This image has some beautiful colour.  I really enjoy that touch of green at the bottom, I think it adds a strong contrast and holds the images'' interest for the viewer.  The transitions between colours are smooth and delicate.<br/> <br/><b>DOF/Focus</b>;<br/>It appears the green is slighting more in focus.  It could be due to the texture difference, but everything seems to be strong and with this being a nearly 2D image the overall focus is nice.<br/> <br/><b>Post</b>;<br/>I don''t know what your post steps are, only basic editing is listed. Overall the image looks well done with only a couple items I will talk about below.<br/> <br/><b>Off Items</b>;<br/>As much as I like this, the Dark tips of the petals that almost blend in the background really distracts the image for me.  Even though I can see the full petals, they give the appearance of incompletion where it should be complete.  Maybe  angling your light stronger, or adding a second smaller light to keep the tips a bit lighter as to show the full effect.  Also, the weakest part of the flower is also the spot of light area creating a blown highlight. My eye tends to be drawn right to that spot because of the darkness of the rest of the image.<br/> <br/><b>Other</b>;<br/>I like your idea, and the border is nice as well.  Your image was very well excepted by the voters.  I believe you did a great job overall, and with a couple minor tweaks it can be a ribbon winner.<br/> <br/>Nice Job<br/> <br/>Andrew ''littlegett''</td>', 'From the Critique Club  How are you doing today?  I am going to touch on a few items with your image. Colour;This image has some beautiful colour.  I really enjoy that touch of green at the bottom, I think it adds a strong contrast and holds the images'' interest for the viewer.  The transitions between colours are smooth and delicate. DOF/Focus;It appears the green is slighting more in focus.  It could be due to the texture difference, but everything seems to be strong and with this being a nearly 2D image the overall focus is nice. Post;I don''t know what your post steps are, only basic editing is listed. Overall the image looks well done with only a couple items I will talk about below. Off Items;As much as I like this, the Dark tips of the petals that almost blend in the background really distracts the image for me.  Even though I can see the full petals, they give the appearance of incompletion where it should be complete.  Maybe  angling your light stronger, or adding a second smaller light to keep the tips a bit lighter as to show the full effect.  Also, the weakest part of the flower is also the spot of light area creating a blown highlight. My eye tends to be drawn right to that spot because of the darkness of the rest of the image. Other;I like your idea, and the border is nice as well.  Your image was very well excepted by the voters.  I believe you did a great job overall, and with a couple minor tweaks it can be a ribbon winner. Nice Job Andrew ''littlegett''', '2007-03-11 14:05:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(3450513, 475215, 63398, '<td valign="top">Taste and vulgarity aside for the moment, it''s abundantly clear as to her position! LOL!! What a hoot, dude!</td>', 'Taste and vulgarity aside for the moment, it''s abundantly clear as to her position! LOL!! What a hoot, dude!', '2007-03-11 14:53:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(3450633, 475244, 14614, '<td valign="top">Hi Karen -- Greetings from the Critique Club ---- <br/> <br/>Great horse shots are a favorite of mine and this one is a great one.  Your central composition balances well with the off-center head, mane, and body.  The DOF (as others have said) is just right as is the exposure.  The eyelashes are one detail that makes my point.<br/> <br/>What may have hurt you in the contest itself is the title -- I think the shot deserves a higher score.  I didn''t vote in this challenge but I would have scored it among my favorites with a 8 -9.  <br/> <br/>Making this better?  That''s a tough one -- one suggestion would be a slightly tigher crop on the left side eliminating the lower left "streek" but then you would have lost perhaps too much of the tail.<br/> <br/>Welcome to DPC - I see you like wildlife and uniquely cropped images -- I enjoyed looking through your portfolio.  <br/> <br/>Please pm me if you have any questions... <br/> <br/>Warm regards,<br/>Theresa</td>', 'Hi Karen -- Greetings from the Critique Club ----  Great horse shots are a favorite of mine and this one is a great one.  Your central composition balances well with the off-center head, mane, and body.  The DOF (as others have said) is just right as is the exposure.  The eyelashes are one detail that makes my point. What may have hurt you in the contest itself is the title -- I think the shot deserves a higher score.  I didn''t vote in this challenge but I would have scored it among my favorites with a 8 -9.   Making this better?  That''s a tough one -- one suggestion would be a slightly tigher crop on the left side eliminating the lower left "streek" but then you would have lost perhaps too much of the tail. Welcome to DPC - I see you like wildlife and uniquely cropped images -- I enjoyed looking through your portfolio.   Please pm me if you have any questions...  Warm regards,Theresa', '2007-03-11 15:39:29.000000', NULL, 0),
