(3453321, 474893, 50695, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>This photo is telling a story. The pad and pen represent a letter that was just written. That letter was put into the envelope. That envelope was sealed with a kiss. Then she suddenly had to go to the loo and so she just left it all lying there. <br/> <br/>The photo is sharp and focused and all that. You probably used a tripod so that you could have a nice small aperture and a nice big depth of field. I like the lighting, particularly on the pen.<br/> <br/>But this photo is only as good as its story, and the story has gaps. For example, the pad and envelope are just floating in black space. Sure, it''s good to remove "distractions" in the background, but having no background is itself a distraction when it doesn''t match the story. Besides, the desk or table or bed(!) could provide some intriguing clues into the characters involved. It might also be good to have signs that she just ripped a page out of that notebook, like some straggling bits of paper. Also, you have a fancy pen but a cheap notebook. What does that mean? You have very few signifiers here, so they should all contribute to your story.<br/> <br/>Can''t seal this with a kiss, sorry! :)</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! This photo is telling a story. The pad and pen represent a letter that was just written. That letter was put into the envelope. That envelope was sealed with a kiss. Then she suddenly had to go to the loo and so she just left it all lying there.  The photo is sharp and focused and all that. You probably used a tripod so that you could have a nice small aperture and a nice big depth of field. I like the lighting, particularly on the pen. But this photo is only as good as its story, and the story has gaps. For example, the pad and envelope are just floating in black space. Sure, it''s good to remove "distractions" in the background, but having no background is itself a distraction when it doesn''t match the story. Besides, the desk or table or bed(!) could provide some intriguing clues into the characters involved. It might also be good to have signs that she just ripped a page out of that notebook, like some straggling bits of paper. Also, you have a fancy pen but a cheap notebook. What does that mean? You have very few signifiers here, so they should all contribute to your story. Can''t seal this with a kiss, sorry! :)', '2007-03-12 12:59:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(3453777, 474879, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Well this is a very creative entry in to the acronym challenge.  I don''t think I would have had a clue about the what the abbreviation was without you spelling it out.  I think that they were a few voters who weren''t happy with the acronym being spelled out but I think it really helped most voters, so good choice.  <br/> <br/>The image itself is very well composed and defiantly grabs the eye.  I think your strong background really draws you into the subject.  The lighting and focus both look good.  I think the image might have scored a little higher if the face on the clock was black or white. <br/> <br/>Overall I think you did a great job on being creative and composing a very nice shot, keep up the good work!</td>', '*Critique Club* Well this is a very creative entry in to the acronym challenge.  I don''t think I would have had a clue about the what the abbreviation was without you spelling it out.  I think that they were a few voters who weren''t happy with the acronym being spelled out but I think it really helped most voters, so good choice.   The image itself is very well composed and defiantly grabs the eye.  I think your strong background really draws you into the subject.  The lighting and focus both look good.  I think the image might have scored a little higher if the face on the clock was black or white.  Overall I think you did a great job on being creative and composing a very nice shot, keep up the good work!', '2007-03-12 15:08:37.000000', NULL, 0),
